There are several dataytypes in SQL

1)INT:-Integer type used for whole numbers.
2)Varchar(100):- Variable length string upto 100 characters.
3)Enum:A string object having a value from a list of permitted value
       Example ENUM('Male','Female','Other')
4)DATE:-Stores date values example date_of_birth DATE
5)TIMESTAMP:-Stores date and time,automatically set to the current timestamp when a row is created
